\frac{AX}{ZB} = \frac{XY}{BC} = \frac{AY}{ZC}
\]
We know that $AX = 6$ cm, $ZB = 18$ cm, and $ZC = 63$ cm. So the ratio of the sides is \[
\frac{AX}{ZB} = \frac{6}{18} = \frac{1}{3}
\]
This ratio also applies to $AY$ and $ZC$. Therefore, \[
\frac{AY}{ZC} = \frac{1}{3}
\]
Since $ZC = 63$ cm, we can find $AY$ by \[
AY = \frac{1}{3} \times 63 = 21 \text{ cm}
\]
